   "text": "I read the structure in sections and wrote the SMILES for each, then joined them.\n\n1. **Left end:** a 2-amino-3,4,5,6-tetrahydropyridine (cyclic amidine) is linked through NH\u2013CH2CH2 to N1 of an indazole.\n2. **Indazole:** C5 carries a carboxamide, C(=O)NH\u2013CH2\u2013.\n3. **Amino-acid core:** the CH2 leads to a CH bearing the sulfonamide NH and a methyl ester. The wedge to the ester gives this carbon @ in the SMILES below.\n4. **Aryl sulfonyl:** the sulfonamide S(=O)(=O) is on a benzene ring with 2,6-dimethyl groups and a 4-O\u2013CH2CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)NH\u2013 chain.\n5. **Linker:** the chain continues NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013N(H). The drawing shows the N without an H, but I took it as NH since it has two bonds.\n6. **Glutamate units:** the linker N is acylated by the first glutamate, which has a CH2CH2CO2tBu side chain, and its \u03b1-NH is acylated by the second glutamate (same side chain). Both wedged centres work out to @ in the SMILES order I used.\n7. **Macrocycle:** the second glutamate's NH is acylated by C(=O)CH2 on a 12-membered tetraaza ring (cyclen, DOTA-type). Each of the other three ring nitrogens carries a CH2CO2tBu arm.\n\nSMILES: C1(NCCn2ncc3cc(C(=O)NC[C@H](NS(=O)(=O)c4c(C)cc(OCCCC(=O)NCCNC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)NC(=O)[C@H](CCC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)NC(=O)CN5CCN(CC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)CCN(CC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)CCN(CC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)CC5)cc4C)C(=O)OC)ccc32)=NCCCC1"
